# Hand-placed leaf clumps for the autumn broadleaf trees. Digits are ramp steps (1 darkest .. 7 brightest); 'o' is the
# darkest edge used under a clump where it overlaps what's behind. Light comes from the top-left: lobes lit on their
# upper-left, a darker crescent under each lobe, the clump's underside darkest. Each is drawn whole, pixel by pixel.

# a big clump: three lobes over two
module clumpA
.......55.........
....5566655..55...
...566666654566...
..56666666545665..
..5666656544565544
.566665544445544.4
.55665544444444443
.5554444444443443.
.4444443433333332.
..4443333332233322
..334333322222221.
...3223222211111..
....2111.1111oo...
end

# a smaller round clump
module clumpB
.....55..5....
...5566556655.
..566666556665
.5666665455654
.56665544445443
55654444444433
.4544444443332
.44443333333321
..333332223221.
...2222211111..
....1o1..1o...
end

# a long low clump for the lower edge of the crown
module clumpC
....55.....55.......
..55665..55665.55...
.5666665566666566...
.56666654666654665..
5666544444554444543.
.55444444444444443332
.444433344433333332.
..33332223322222221.
...2211..112111111..
.....oo...ooo.......
end

# loose leaves at the crown's edge, so the silhouette breaks up the way a real crown does
module tipA
.55.
5665
.54.
..3.
end
module tipB
5.5
656
.4.
end
module tipC
.5.
564
453
.3.
end
